  "content": {
    "title": "CSU vs Michigan State recap as Rams just miss big upset",
    "text": "Updated March 20, 2026, 8:48 p.m. MTThe 2026 Women's NCAA Tournament is underway.Norman, Oklahoma, was the site for a No. 5-12 March Madness matchup between No. 5 Michigan State of the Big Ten and No. 12 Colorado State of the Mountain West.The Coloradoan brought you live updates, scores and highlights from the CSU vs. Michigan State game. Follow along. No. 5 Michigan State beats No. 12 Colorado StateAn incredible first-round game came down to the final shot. No. 5 Michigan State was an 18.5-point favorite but only wins 65-62 over No. 12 Colorado State.Brooke Carlson had a career-high 26 points for CSU, hitting 8 of 17 shots (3-5 from 3-point range). She also had six rebounds and three assists.Grace VanSlooten had 18 points and 10 rebounds for the Spartans. Kennedy Blair scored 18 points and had three blocks.— Kevin Lytle Game-tying 3-pointer missesWow what a finish. Colorado State gets the ball with a chance to tie. Rams draw up a play for senior Hannah Ronsiek and get her open in the corner, but her would-be tying 3-pointer misses.Michigan State escapes 65-62.— Kevin Lytle Career-high for Brooke CarlsonBrooke Carlson hits a 3-pointer and she has a career-high 26 points to keep CSU in it. Michigan State ball up 65-62 with 39.1 seconds to go.— Kevin Lytle Michigan State holding onSpartans lead 65-59 with 41.2 seconds to go. CSU ball.— Kevin Lytle Crunch timeMichigan State leads 64-59 with 45.1 seconds to go. It was called CSU ball but after a long review it goes to Michigan State.— Kevin Lytle Brooke Carlson keeping CSU in itBrooke Carlson hits a 3-pointer and then a circus shot of a layup and Rams are hanging in the game.Michigan State up 62-57 with 1:44 to go.— Kevin Lytle Michigan State makes a pushA little 6-2 run and Michigan State has held Colorado State scoreless for more than 2 minutes.Spartans lead 58-52 with 4:54 to go. It's Michigan State's largest lead of the game.— Kevin Lytle Four fouls on Kennedy BlairKennedy Blair has 14 points for Michigan State but now she has four fouls with 7 minutes left in the game.— Kevin Lytle Four fouls on Marta LeimaneCSU's Marta Leimane picked up her fourth foul late in the third quarter. Leimane doesn't put up big numbers, but is a big connector on offense and defense.— Kevin Lytle All tied heading to fourth quarterWhat a finish we have ahead. No. 12 Colorado State is tied 47-47 with No. 5 Michigan State after three quarters.— Kevin Lytle Jalyn Brown finally hits a Michigan State 3-pointerJalyn Brown started the game hitting a 3-pointer on Michigan State's first possession. The Spartans then missed 16 in a row from deep.That streak was finally snapped in the third quarter when Brown hit another. Michigan State is now 2-17 from deep.Colorado State leads 41-38 with 3:48 left in the third quarter.— Kevin Lytle Michigan State cannot score on Colorado StateCSU has a top-10 scoring defense in the nation. Even with Bargesser out, the Rams are stifling the Spartans.Michigan State hit its first 3-pointer of the game and has now missed 15 in a row. Michigan State averages more than 80 points per game and has just 33 through nearly 25 minutes of action.— Kevin Lytle See photos from Michigan State and Colorado StateCheck out some photos from the first half!— Kevin Lytle Colorado State controlling Michigan StateThis is how the Rams want it. CSU is dropping deep into the paint defensively, almost daring Michigan State to shoot jumpers. Spartans are shooting just 11-32 (34%) overall and 1-14 on 3-pointers. Rams are even winning the rebounding battle 20-15.CSU has eight turnovers (the Rams average just 10 per game) but it's only led to three Michigan State points.Brooke Carlson has 11 points, five rebounds and an assist for CSU. Grace VanSlooten has nine points and seven rebounds for the Spartans.— Kevin Lytle Underdog Colorado State leads Michigan StateMichigan State is an 18.5-point favorite and Colorado State has a 29-27 halftime lead.Rams playing it at the pace they want it. Michigan State averages more than 80 points per games but Rams have held the Spartans to 11-32 (34%) shooting and 1-14 (7%) from 3-point range.— Kevin Lytle Sparty and CAM dance offWhat's an NCAA Tournament game without a good dance off?— Kevin Lytle Who is Brooke Carlson? Meet CSU's rising starBrooke Carlson off to a great start for upset-minded Colorado State. She's at 11 points midway through the second quarter, which is her season average.Carlson is a 5-foot-8 sophomore guard from Batavia, Illinois. She was on the All-MW Freshman team last season as she averaged 7.7 points and 2.6 assists per game.Carlson was a 4A All-State first-team player in 2023-24 in Illinois. She averaged 22.4 points, 3.9 steals, 3.7 rebounds and 2.5 assists as a senior. She was Batavia High School's all-time leading scorer with a whopping 2,225 points. She also led in career steals and assists.— Kevin Lytle Michigan State leads after first quarterRams start really well, Michigan State settles in. It's Michigan State 16-13 after the first quarter.All told, a good quarter from the Rams. The pace was mostly slow (how CSU wants it) and Michigan State wasn't overwhelming inside.CSU weathered the early fouls to Bragg.— Kevin Lytle Brooke Carlson is cookingCSU sophomore guard Brooke Carlson has P4 pace and is causing problems. She has six early points for the Rams.She's a big, big talent.— Kevin Lytle Hannah Ronsiek sparks early Colorado State runA great start for the Rams. Hannah Ronsiek hits a middy then drains a 3-pointer to help spark a 9-0 run.CSU is up 9-3 with 4:52 left in the first quarter.— Kevin Lytle Two fouls on Madelyn BraggCSU big Madelyn Bragg picks up her second foul of the game just over 4 minutes in. Both were on the offensive end.That's not good for the Rams, who are undersized and very limited in depth.— Kevin Lytle Michigan State starting lineupHere is the starting 5 for the Spartans:Guard Rashunda Jones (11.8 ppg)Guard Jalyn Brown (11.1 ppg)Guard Kennedy Blair (14.4 ppg)Forward Grace VanSlooten (15 ppg)Center Ines Sotelo (6.8 ppg)— Kevin Lytle Colorado State starting lineupHere is the starting 5 for the Rams:Guard Kloe Froebe (10.7 ppg)Guard Brooke Carlson (11.3 ppg)Guard Marta Leimane (5.0 ppg)Guard Hannah Ronsiek (7.7 ppg)Center Madelyn Bragg (8.2 ppg)— Kevin Lytle Almost time for March MadnessTip time is almost here for Colorado State and Michigan State!— Kevin Lytle Colorado State fans ready in NormanCSU fans getting ready for the game in Norman. This is CSU's first Women's NCAA Tournament game since 2016.— Kevin Lytle Brooke Carlson, Kloe Froebe lead Colorado StateWith Bargesser out, two sophomores grow even more important for CSU.Brooke Carlson is CSU's leading scorer among players available at 11.3 points per game. The speedy guard also leads the team in assists (3.1 per game) and steals with 46.\"We go as Brooke goes,\" CSU coach Ryun Williams said this week.Kloe Froebe averages 10.7 points and a team-high 6.8 rebounds per game.Those two sophomores (who are close friends) are key for CSU hopes against Michigan State.— Kevin Lytle Michigan State on Colorado StateHere's what Michigan State coach Robyn Fralick said about CSU: \"Colorado State is a really good team. I mean, 27 wins is a lot of wins over the course of a season. What stands out about them is their patience, their discipline. They do a really good job of executing on both sides of the ball.\"Obviously we have pretty contrasting styles of play, so we're going to have to — we have to have a level of patience. One of the phrases we've been using is 'aggressive patience.' We still have to play the way we love to play, but we also have to understand there's a discipline and a patience to the possessions. That's how you execute at a high level. Making sure that our possessions have a meaningfulness behind them. We don't want to have empty possessions.\"— Kevin Lytle Colorado State star Lexus Bargesser outCSU is without Indiana transfer Lexus Bargesser against the Spartans. Bargesser, a senior, was named the Mountain West Newcomer of the Year after starring in her first and lone season as a Ram.Bargesser averaged more than 15 points per game, to go with 5.9 rebounds, 2.8 assists per game and 1.3 steals per game.She was injured in the Mountain West semifinals and will miss the remainder of the season, however long that goes, for the Rams.— Kevin Lytle Michigan State's NCAA Tournament resumeThe Spartans are in the Big Dance for the third season in a row and 21st time overall. The Spartans are 20-20 all-time in NCAA Tournament games.Michigan State is an at-large team from the Big Ten. The conference landed 12 bids into the Big Dance. Michigan State went 11-8 to finish seventh in the Big Ten.The Spartans are 22-8 overall and No. 17 in the NCAA's NET rankings and No. 21 in BartTorvik's metrics.— Kevin Lytle Colorado State's NCAA Tournament resumeThe Rams are in the Big Dance for the first time since 2016 and seventh time overall. The Rams are 5-6 all-time in NCAA Tournament games.CSU is in as the automatic bid for the Mountain West via winning the conference tournament. CSU went 15-5 in MW play to finish in a tie for second and as the No. 3 seed went 3-0 to win the conference tournament.CSU is 27-7 overall, the second-most wins in a season under 14th-year coach Ryun Williams. The Rams are No. 70 in the NCAA's NET rankings and No. 69 in BartTorvik's metrics.— Kevin Lytle Colorado State basketball March Madness game vs Michigan State timeDate: Friday, March 20Time: 5:30 p.m. MT/6:30 p.m. CTLocation: Lloyd Noble Center, Norman, Oklahoma— Kevin Lytle How to watch, stream Colorado State vs Michigan State March Madness gameTV channel: ESPNewsStreaming: ESPN+, FuboWatch CSU vs Michigan State on Fubo (free trial available)The Colorado State vs. Michigan State first-round Women's NCAA Tournament game will air on ESPNews. It can be streamed on ESPN+ and Fubo, which offers free trials to potential subscribers.— Kevin Lytle Michigan State basketball vs Colorado State oddsHere are the betting odds, according to BetMGM:Spread: Michigan State by 18.5 points.Over/under: 134.5 points.Moneyline: CSU (+1490), Michigan State (-4800).— Kevin LytleSports reporter Kevin Lytle can be found on social media on X, Instagram and Threads @Kevin_Lytle and on Bluesky.",
